'' A procedure named as a type -- 'dim a as ns.F', 'dim b as G' -- is fbc's error 14 on
'' both lines (fbc-modern 1.20, 2026-10-22). tiko took the procedure's own type and declared
'' a 4-byte variable: 'dim a as win.MSG' meant sys/win's Msg function, not windows.bi's
'' 48-byte MSG. A real type and a variable's sizeof in the same unit are untouched; each
'' error is reported once.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -c tests/diagnostics/src/proc-as-type.bas -o tests/diagnostics/src/proc-as-type.o
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 1
'' EXPECT-OUT: proc-as-type.bas(12,10): error TKO0997: 'ns.f' is a procedure, not a type
'' EXPECT-OUT: proc-as-type.bas(13,10): error TKO0997: 'g' is a procedure, not a type
'' EXPECT-NOT: TKO0808
'' EXPECT-MAX-DIAG: 2
